      "treatment_summary": "Antibiotics at another hospital at 2 months (fever did not subside); fever and rash abated a little without specific treatment; currently followed up without routine medications; sometimes admitted at local hospitals for severe oral ulcers and poor feeding; a TNF blocker would be given if symptoms worsened.",
      "disease_label_as_stated": "HA20 (infantile familial HA20; initially suspected neonatal lupus erythematosus); also neurofibromatosis (NF1 variant)",
